{"seq":13,"trial_id":"v03-pilot-2026-10/hermes-haiku-gbrain-verbs-told-mu-v03-dev/sy-02-marrow-agrisupply-sites/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-29T19:19:39.904Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"ceee99e9cc7e0b3e78890dd106a7f45d12b8fc9aaa06ddf845c3189b844c599a","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","text":"Pree, here's what I found on Marrow Agrisupply sites in #central-team, which you can see.\n\n1. Eastbank: June 9 thread. Hollis says ticket PD-4821 has the Eastbank receiving-door import attached, and the door labels (E1/E2) don't match the booking sheet (01/02). Source: #central-team, 2026-06-09 10:46, Hollis Mbeki.\n2. Pine Crossing: same thread. You reported the appointment screen shows only the afternoon shift, so a morning receiver can't book. Source: #central-team, 2026-06-09 10:48, your message.\n\nThe June 9 escalation also mentions \"new stores\" and three rows marked \"waiting\" in the rollout tracker, but the store names aren't in the channel, so I can't list them.\n\nI checked the shared files and the knowledge brain too. The Central cheat sheet and the handoff digest mention Marrow only as the ag account (door 4 message, feature request FR-882 for fertilizer sheds), with no site names. The handoff digest's Salina North yard is tied to a different account, so I left it out.\n\nFor the full store list, PD-4821 or the rollout tracker would have the missing names."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
